      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like how this removes the need to enforce a specific ordering, nice work! But, I\u0027m not sure if it should be a property of the token model.\n\nIn my opinion, a payload class is actually an implementation detail of how the fernet token provider encapsulates payload structures for different token types. In that case, I wonder if this piece wouldn\u0027t be a better fit in the fernet token provider and not the token formatter.\n\nAlso, do we expect other token providers to reuse these exact payload classes? Originally, we thought we might be able to reuse this for JWT support, but with how JWT works I don\u0027t think a serialized payload is necessary (JWT can accomplish this with key-value pairs at the expense of a larger token ID).",
      "revId": "5c2241c3edab388fb87653b4b579ec97f22e9d28",
