      "writtenOn": "2019-01-03T20:36:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can remove this if we take the following approach:\n\n\n  def _determine_payload_class_from_token(self, token):\n      if token.oauth_scoped:\n          return self.token_formatters.OauthScopedPayload\n      elif token.trust_scoped:\n          return self.token_formatters.TrustScopedPayload\n      elif token.is_federated:\n          if token.project_scoped:\n              return self.token_formatters.FederatedProjectScopedPayload\n          elif token.domain_scoped:\n              return self.token_formatters.FederatedDomainScopedPayload\n          elif token.unscoped:\n              return self.token_formatters.FederatedUnscopedPayload\n      elif token.application_credential_id:\n          return self.token_formatters.ApplicationCredentialScopedPayload\n      elif token.project_scoped:\n          return self.token_formatters.ProjectScopedPayload\n      elif token.domain_scoped:\n          return self.token_formatters.DomainScopedPayload\n      elif token.system_scoped:\n          return self.token_formatters.SystemScopedPayload\n      else:\n          return self.token_formatters.UnscopedPayload\n\n  def generate_id_and_issued_at(self, token):\n      payload_class \u003d self._determine_payload_class_from_token(token)\n\nWhich has the advantage of keeping payload details specific to fernet out of the token model. Also, it keeps the token model from having a dependency on the token_formatter module, since we have that available as a property of the Provider instance here.",
